  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one data point (RNA-only PCA singleprofile at ~48.5% accuracy), so evidence is very sparse. The most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal at all, which determines whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing in later experiments. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly tests this: if image-only accuracy is competitive or better, multimodal configurations become high-priority; if it is poor, we should focus remaining budget on RNA encoder and profile improvements. Using ResNet50 (a standard, well-transferred backbone) keeps the test clean and avoids confounding with an untested ViT encoder. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the modality axis, which is the highest-leverage design decision given the limited 8-experiment budget remaining."
}

